  "title": "Coast Guard Rescues 37 After Fishing Boat Capsizes, Sinks in the Eastern Pacific Ocean",
  "description": "A rescue swimmer from a U.S. Coast Guard cutter swims to the aid of a crewman from the Ecuadorian fishing vessel Marujita, who clings to the hull of the capsized vessel approximately 336 miles southeast of Clipperton Island August 7, 2019. The crewman was one of 25 crew members and 12 Coast Guardsmen who abandoned the Marujita and were rescued by the crew of the Coast Guard cutter after the 160-foot fishing boat listed and capsized. (U.S. Coast Guard courtesy video/Released)",
